      "comment" : "Button of the sleep timer sheet that stops the running timer.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cancelar temporizador"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Case sensitive" : {
      "comment" : "A part of a substitution rule's spoken summary: capital and small letters are told apart.\nTitle of the switch in the substitution rule editor that makes the pattern tell capital and small letters apart."
    },
    "Case sensitive matching" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Case sensitive switch in the substitution rule editor."
    },
    "Check the criteria above, then %@." : {
      "comment" : "What Find Duplicate Books shows before its first scan. %@ is the title of the scan button."
    },
    "Choose a voice for reading. Change takes effect immediately." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the voice pop-up in the Voice settings."
    },
    "Choose no per-book control, one picker for both directions, or one menu with separate forward and backward pickers" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Navigation unit controls pop-up in the Playback settings."
    },
    "Chooses what a book opened from the list does when it ends." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Reading List's When a book ends pop-up button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Elige qué hace un libro abierto desde la lista al terminar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chooses where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs. %@ keeps them in its Logs folder, beside your books, where they move with the library and sync with it when it is in the cloud. %@ keeps them in %@, which never syncs. A change applies from the next line written; logs already written are not moved." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint and tooltip of the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings. %1$@ and %2$@ are the names of its two choices, as the pop-up lists them, and %3$@ is the folder's path on this Mac, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Chooses where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs. %1$@ keeps them in its Logs folder, beside your books, where they move with the library and sync with it when it is in the cloud. %2$@ keeps them in %3$@, which never syncs. A change applies from the next line written; logs already written are not moved."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chooses where the next book opens: in this window or a new one. A book open in another window comes forward, and with %@ chosen, this window closes." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Open the next book in pop-up button in Settings, Playback, also shown under it. %@ is the name of its choice This Window.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Elige dónde se abre el siguiente libro: en esta ventana o en una nueva. Un libro abierto en otra ventana pasa al frente y, si eliges %@, esta ventana se cierra."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chooses where this feed's next article opens." : {
